Hello friends,

Yesterday, I uploaded my APC daemon to the sunsite.unc.edu
/pub/Linux/Incoming.

The apcd daemon is able to communicate with APC SmartUPS in "smart"
mode via RS232 line.  The daemon is collecting data from UPS. If the
power is going down, users are notified about this fact. If power is
not restored during the timeout, apcd will shutdown the system and
switch-off the UPS.  There soon will be some kind of the client for
displaying the UPS data (line voltage, UPS load, battery capacity
etc.).

