I've uploaded at version 2.8 to sunsite.unc.edu; it should arrive
at the correct places soon.

There is one security fix:  All earlier versions of at allowed somebody
with write access to the /var/spool/atjobs directory (i.e. a cracker
who had obtained userid 'bin' in most installations) to gain
root access.  This has been fixed.

There is also one usability enhancment, thanks to David Parsons
(orc@pell.com):  Instead of long job names, at now uses shorter
job numbers.

Following is the lsm entry.

