               -------------------------------

[I noticed that sunsite did not have the most recent version of scilab,
so I ftp'd it from ftp.inria.fr.  I have unpacked the binary
distribution and have tried out a few things.  I didn't do anything with
the sources except gzip -d to be sure they weren't entirely garbled. 
I don't know what the fixes/improvements were - CHANGES had not been
updated.  The rest of this comes from the 2.1 release announcement. - jrv]

    Scilab is a matrix-based scientific software package resembling
Matlab and Xmath. Scilab contains hundreds of built-in mathematical
functions, rich  data structures (including polynomials, rationals,
linear systems, lists, etc...)  and comes with a number of specific
toolboxes for control, signal processing, ...

    As usual,  Scilab  is distributed free, in source code format,
as well as in binary formats. Scilab can be obtained by anonymous
ftp from "ftp.inria.fr" (Internet #192.93.2.54), directory
"INRIA/Projects/Meta2/Scilab".  
[...but look at a sunsite mirror if it's closer -jrv]

    Scilab has been developed for the Unix/Xwindow environment and is
available and tested on the following systems:

	SUN Sparc (Solaris and SUN.OS)
	DEC Alpha OSF
	DEC Mips Ultrix
	IBM RS6000 AIX
	HP 9000 HPUX
	SGI Mips IRIX
	PC Linux

    Scilab 2.0 has been a great success. We have  received hundreds of
e-mails: requesting information, suggesting improvements, pointing out
bugs, etc... We like to thank all those  who have been helping us
improve and develop Scilab.

    Even though the Scilab language is in large part Matlab compatible
(in particular for basic operations), Scilab is NOT a matlab clone.
Unlike some other free matlab-like packages, our intention  is not to
always  seek  matlab  compatibility.  Scilab  has a  rich  data
structure  (polynomials,  rationals, lists,...) and  translating  a
matlab  program  into Scilab (which  in  most  cases requires  very
little effort) usually  leads to a much shorter and simpler code.

