This document gives an English description of what has changed in the
most recent version of the Linux FAQ.

Comments on and submissions for the FAQ are strongly encouraged and
welcomed - I don't have time to read every article in col.*, and
thus need your assistance to spot the FAQ-threads that I miss.


Changes March - May 1995:

New Questions:
Q4.1.  How can I get Linux to work with my large disk ?

Modified Questions:
Q3.6.  Can I run Microsoft Windows ...  Mentioned possible dosemu support.
Q1.3.  Does it run on my computer ?     Said no multiprocessor support.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   68K X server; new URLs in text.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   MacLinux rumoured dead.
Q4.9.  Is there something like Stacker  DouBle FTP location changed.
Q6.8.  ... weird characters ...         Removed suggestion of ^O in prompt.
Q7.7.  ... more than 3 serial ports ... Just can't *use* all at once.
Q7.9.  How do I remap my keyboard ...   kbd-0.xx.tar.gz version number.
Q9.12. EXT2-fs warning: maximal count   e2fsprogs version number.
Q9.15. ... different physical/logical   Moved much stuff to new Q4.1.
Q10.1. Does Linux support X Windows ?   XFree86 version is 3.1.1.


Changes January - March 1995:

New Questions:
Q5.12. Where can I find `kermit' for Linux ?
Q6.14. How do I get LILO to boot the vmlinux file ?

Modified Questions:
Q1.2.  What software does it support ?  Gave iBCS2 FTP location.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   Information on ARM/Acorn ports added.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   Mentioned PowerPC FAQ.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   Incorrect list addresses fixed.
Q2.1.  Where can I get the HOWTOs ...   HOWTO list & maintainer updated.
Q2.3.  What newsgroups are there ...    New groups, changed throughout FAQ.
Q2.3.  What newsgroups are there ...    col.announce address changed.
Q2.5.  Where can I get ... by FTP ?     ftp.cc.gatech.edu, ftp.cdrom.com.
Q2.9.  Are the newsgroups archived ...  Only col.announce is nowadays.
Q3.3.  Can I use my Stacked/DBLSPC/etc. Info about `thsfs' kernel module.
Q3.5.  Can I access ... Mac filesystems xhsfs is becoming a kernel module.
Q3.7.  boot ... from OS/2 Boot Manager  Slightly simpler in OS/2 "warp" 3.0.
Q4.5.  My swap area isn't working.      Tidied up mention of /etc/rc.
Q4.6.  How do I remove LILO ...         Say that FDISK /MBR is undocumented.
Q5.2.  Has anyone ported / compiled ... Added info re LSM search engine.
Q5.2.  Has anyone ported / compiled ... col.announce address changed.
Q5.4.  ... compiler [for a 486] on 386  Added Pentium-GCC (but discouraged).
Q5.11. Where can I get `lint' ...       Mentioned lclint.
Q6.8.  [screen full] of weird chars     Suggested putting ^O in prompt.
Q7.2.  How do I switch virtual consoles Recent kernels alloc dynamically.
Q7.10. How do I get NUM LOCK [on]       Tidied up mention of /etc/rc.
Q9.8.  No utmp entry.  You must exec    Tidied up mention of /etc/rc.
Q9.11. ...mounting unchecked filesystem Tidied up mention of /etc/rc.
Q9.14. df says Cannot read table ...    Tidied up mention of /etc/rc.
Q12.2. What to put in a [help request]  Applies to emailed queries too.
Q13.3. Authorship and acknowledgements  New HOWTO coordinator.
Q13.4. Disclaimer and Copyright         Fixed spelling typo.


All question numbers should refer to the numbering in the new edition
in each case (eg, for the January to February changes the numbers
would refer to the February edition).

