Heia,

I re-uploaded SAR and Kiss to sunsite and tsx. And just so soon after the last
release! I had made a dumb mistake in the Getline version of Kiss; it failed
to read the input from e.g. a pipe. So, with the one fix, here's Kiss 0.11. I
also re-uploaded SAR, since this package uses Kiss.

What is is? Kiss is my "keep it simple shell", a-la tcsh or bash but much less
sophisticated. Kiss however has lots of built-in commands, such as "ls",
"mount" or "touch". That makes Kiss perfectly suitable for a search-and-rescue
disk: you just put Kiss on the diskette and leave out "ls", "mv", "rm" etc..
SAR is just that: a maker of search-and-rescue disks, which relies on Kiss as
the shell interpreter. SAR creates a bootable root-login diskette (or a set of
two diskettes, if instructed so).

Where to get it? The primary ftp site is still ftp.icce.rug.nl:/pub/unix,
files SAR* and kiss*. Furthermore, you'll find SAR and Kiss on sunsite and
tsx; search under "shells" or "backup" or "sbin" directories.

K.
